{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr47rt5f7u1","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"EWM vision on ls20 unblocks program synthesis but not valid synthesis","summary":"Live ls20 EWM run with vision ON (qwen35b-arc, vision-capable) vs prior text-only run (ornith35b-arc). Result: vision flipped program_adopted false to true -- the agent left reactive RECOVER mode and entered SYNTHESIZE/EXECUTE, adopting a world-model program the text-only model never could. But the adopted program mispredicted all 80 observed transitions (divergences=80, empirical pass_rate 0.0), so 0/7 levels cleared, same as text-only and the reactive baseline (three-way tie on levels). So vision moves the bottleneck downstream: from cannot-author-a-program to authors-a-program-that-does-not-match-ls20-dynamics. Enabling fix required: qwen35b-arc is a thinking model; with thinking ON it spends the whole token budget in the reasoning field and returns empty content (finish_reason=length even at 4000 tokens), so it can never emit a fenced program. Disabling thinking via a new ARC_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT env knob (reasoning_effort:none on the /v1 endpoint) is what let synthesis engage at all. Multimodality verified: model correctly named the changed cell in a 3x3 BEFORE|AFTER|DIFF composite via both /v1 image_url parts and native /api/chat images. Scorecard 3cab1596-cd3c-4914-8aab-7090e831a8c4.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T00:47:32.691Z","vec":[-0.016957128420472145,-0.034358344972133636,-0.00265093264169991,0.0187680684030056,0.11414703726768494,-0.03116629086434841,-0.06043357774615288,0.06355905532836914,0.02264852449297905,0.029028214514255524,-0.014316637068986893,-0.06732131540775299,0.034331727772951126,0.007401222363114357,0.020422471687197685,0.08309907466173172,0.0769539549946785,-0.0832362025976181,-0.07528378814458847,-0.008378923870623112,0.04630957171320915,-0.04897434264421463,0.034699589014053345,-0.004509531427174807,-0.0141781857237219